# Production demo profile — everything real, no mocks.
#
# `.env.example` is the DEVELOPMENT profile: fake LLM, hash embeddings, fake
# Redis. It exists so the pipeline can be exercised for free. This file is the
# opposite: every component is the real one, which is what gets demoed.
#
#   cp .env.production.example .env
#   docker compose up -d redis qdrant
#   docker compose --profile observability up -d
#   uv run uvicorn assistant.main:app
# then fill the (empty) knowledge base live — see Knowledge base below.
#
# Full runbook: docs/project/demo-runbook.md

# --- LLM: real -----------------------------------------------------------
ASSISTANT_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
ASSISTANT_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4.1-nano
ASSISTANT_LLM_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Embeddings: real ----------------------------------------------------
# 1536-dim vectors from OpenAI, not the offline hash stand-in. Switching
# providers changes the vector width: the collection is recreated on the next
# ingest, and previously indexed documents are gone — re-ingest what you need.
# Cost: ~$0.02 per 1M tokens — a typical repo's docs are well under a cent.
ASSISTANT_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai
ASSISTANT_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
ASSISTANT_EMBEDDING_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Infra: real ---------------------------------------------------------
# Real Redis (sessions survive a restart) and real Qdrant (on-disk vectors,
# dashboard at localhost:6333/dashboard). Both from docker-compose.yml.
ASSISTANT_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
ASSISTANT_QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:6333
ASSISTANT_QDRANT_COLLECTION=docs

# --- Knowledge base ------------------------------------------------------
# Starts empty — nothing pre-loads it. Fill it live during the demo by
# asking the assistant: "ingest the docs from owner/name". Its ingest_repo
# tool indexes the repo's .md/.txt/.rst as owner/repo/path sources; the UI's
# Documents panel still handles ad-hoc file drops. The same read-only PAT as
# the MCP server works here; without it only public repos can be ingested.
# ASSISTANT_GITHUB_TOKEN=github_pat_...

# --- Agent ---------------------------------------------------------------
ASSISTANT_AGENT_BACKEND=custom

# --- MCP tool servers: real ----------------------------------------------
# Two servers, both real:
#   code   -> regex search + file reads over THIS repository (no public server
#             does this — GitHub's searches GitHub, not your working copy)
#   github -> GitHub's own hosted MCP server, real PRs and issues
#
# The PAT: github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens -> fine-grained token,
# read-only, scoped to the repos you will demo. Contents: Read. Pull requests:
# Read. Issues: Read. Nothing else. It authenticates the header below.
#
# COST WARNING: every tool's JSON schema rides in EVERY prompt. The full
# GitHub server exposes ~44 tools (~12,900 tokens/prompt, ~$0.0019 a turn);
# scoping to the two toolsets the demo actually calls cuts that sharply. Keep
# it trimmed or the demo pays ~12x per question for an identical answer.
#
# Toolset scoping on the hosted server (both documented upstream):
#   - `X-MCP-Toolsets: pull_requests,issues` header to combine toolsets
#   - `/readonly` URL suffix for read-only; `/x/{toolset}` for a single one,
#     e.g. https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/x/pull_requests/readonly
# The endpoint 401s before it routes, so the exact path could not be verified
# here without a PAT — if a scoped URL misbehaves, fall back to /mcp/readonly
# and scope with the header alone.
#
# Option A — hosted (no Docker; endpoint verified live, 401 without auth):
# ASSISTANT_MCP_SERVERS='[{"name":"code","command":"{python}","args":["-m","assistant.mcp_servers.code_search"]},{"name":"github","transport":"http","url":"https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/readonly","headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer github_pat_...","X-MCP-Toolsets":"pull_requests,issues"}}]'
#
# Option B — local container (works offline once pulled, PAT still required):
# ASSISTANT_MCP_SERVERS='[{"name":"code","command":"{python}","args":["-m","assistant.mcp_servers.code_search"]},{"name":"github","command":"docker","args":["run","-i","--rm","-e","GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN","-e","GITHUB_TOOLSETS","ghcr.io/github/github-mcp-server"],"env":{"GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN":"github_pat_...","GITHUB_TOOLSETS":"pull_requests,issues"}}]'
#
# Leaving ASSISTANT_MCP_SERVERS unset falls back to the DEV default: real code
# search plus the mocked GitHub server. That fallback is a development
# convenience — it is not the production demo.
ASSISTANT_MCP_ENABLED=true

# --- Observability: real -------------------------------------------------
# Traces to local Jaeger (localhost:16686), metrics scraped by Prometheus,
# dashboard in Grafana (localhost:3000). Started by the observability profile.
ASSISTANT_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
# Optional cloud lenses on the same spans (docs/reference/logfire-langfuse.md):
# ASSISTANT_LOGFIRE_TOKEN=pylf_v1_eu_...
# ASSISTANT_LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-...
# ASSISTANT_LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-...
# ASSISTANT_LANGFUSE_HOST=https://cloud.langfuse.com
ASSISTANT_LOG_JSON=true

# --- Guards --------------------------------------------------------------
# A shared demo URL with a real key behind it should not be open. Set a token
# and the UI picks it up from ?token=<token>.
# ASSISTANT_AUTH_TOKEN=change-me
ASSISTANT_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=true
ASSISTANT_RATE_LIMIT_TURNS_PER_MINUTE=20
ASSISTANT_RATE_LIMIT_UPLOADS_PER_HOUR=50
